.Trashes
**/.DS_Store

# Data — annotation exports contain personal annotator names
data/annotation/doccano/*
!data/annotation/doccano/README.md

# data/processed/, data/silver/, data/title-length/, data/eval/, data/gold/, data/iaa/,
# data/adjudication/, data/heuristics/ are ALL tracked. The former group was previously ignored as
# "reproducible from tracked scripts," but that's true only in principle — regenerating
# data/silver/silver_spans.jsonl (2026-07-10) took ~64 min (FLERT sub-classification over ~34K
# statement-of-responsibility segments) and needs two large external files (a 1.3GB ratings CSV +
# a 1.3GB parquet) that live in the separate gemea project, not in this repo — so "reproducible"
# silently also meant "have gemea's output directory available," not guaranteed by cloning this
# repo alone. Not worth the regeneration cost or the external dependency for files this size
# (silver_spans.jsonl + gliner_dataset_silver.jsonl together are ~32MB) — tracked directly instead.
# data/gold/, data/iaa/, data/adjudication/, data/heuristics/ were always tracked: manually reviewed
# ground truth (gold labels, IAA scores, adjudication decisions, sr04 true_class), not reproducible
# from scripts alone (their raw input, the Doccano exports below, is PII-excluded), and contain no
# PII themselves. See notes/fiz/bibner-werk/data-reorg-plan.md (historical — describes the original
# split, superseded 2026-07-10 for the four now-tracked directories).

# Runtime logs
data/logs/

